484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The SMB beta indicates the comovement of the stock with the outperformance of small companies \(by market cap\) compared to large companies. Only TSLA, AAPL, KO, and LMT have significant SMB betas. TSLA is small-like \(blue\), despite being one of the biggest companies in the world. On the other hand, AAPL, KO, and LMT are all large-like \(red\), which matches with their market cap. When small companies do well, Tesla will outperform, and when large companies do well, AAPL, KO and LMT will outperform the estimations of more naive models. The HML beta indicates the comovement of the stock with the outperformance of high-value companies \(by Book-to-market\) compared to low-value \(aka growth\) companies. All HML betas are significant at the 1% level. XOM is strongly value, with an HML beta near 1. ROST, KO, LMT are also value companies, while TSLA and AAPL are growth companies. Historically, value has outperformed growth, but had higher negative returns in market downturns, justifying the premium.)
/E (The SMB beta indicates the comovement of the stock with the outperformance of small companies \(by market cap\) compared to large companies. Only TSLA, AAPL, KO, and LMT have significant SMB betas. TSLA is small-like \(blue\), despite being one of the biggest companies in the world. On the other hand, AAPL, KO, and LMT are all large-like \(red\), which matches with their market cap. When small companies do well, Tesla will outperform, and when large companies do well, AAPL, KO and LMT will outperform the estimations of more naive models. The HML beta indicates the comovement of the stock with the outperformance of high-value companies \(by Book-to-market\) compared to low-value \(aka growth\) companies. All HML betas are significant at the 1% level. XOM is strongly value, with an HML beta near 1. ROST, KO, LMT are also value companies, while TSLA and AAPL are growth companies. Historically, value has outperformed growth, but had higher negative returns in market downturns, justifying the premium.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [17]
>>
